  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Fact-Based and Data-Driven Migration Governance and Management in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to Strengthen fact-based and data-driven migration governance through the review of the National Migration Policy and the development of a National GCM Implementation Plan. The paucity of disaggregated and up-to-date data on the realities of migration; its application to policy making, implementation and practice; and its impact on potential, current and returned migrants (especially female migrants) and the realisation of their rights are critical gaps that require addressing. To this end, this joint programme will seek to achieve strengthened migration governance through enhanced institutional capacity, an Improved National Migration Governance Framework, and the development of the National implementation plan on the GCM. The process will include the enhancement of the knowledge and skill set of relevant stakeholders on existing dynamics of migration; building their capacity on migration data management and coordination; contributing to the review of the National Migration Policy, and developing the GCM implementation plan which will enable the localisation the Global Compact for Migration, being the bedrock on ensuring the protection, fulfilment, and realisation of migrant&apos;s rights, irrespective of their gender.</narrative>
  </description>
